{
  "id": "Compound::DB01329 - Gene::10864",
  "verbalization": "Cefoperazone, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is shown to bind to multiple Slc22 family members, including Slc22a11 and Slc22a8, which are involved in the transport of organic anions and cations. These transporters are functionally linked to Slc22a7, a member of the Slc22 family that is primarily involved in the transport of organic anions. The evidence suggests that Cefoperazone may inhibit the activity of Slc22a7 by binding to its transporters, thereby affecting the uptake of organic anions, including those that are substrates of Cefoperazone. The overlapping roles of Slc22a11 and Slc22a8 in the transport process, along with their shared participation in the transport of organic anions, support the hypothesis that Cefoperazone may act through a common mechanism involving these transporters. The final scores from the paths indicate a strong, albeit variable, level of confidence in this relationship, suggesting that the observed interactions are biologically relevant and consistent with a mechanistic link between Cefoperazone and Slc22a7.",
